tortoise-wow: ElunaCreatureAI falls back to the native AI when the creature has no Eluna state, instead of calling through a null pointer.

Every hook in ElunaCreatureAI did me->GetEluna()->Hook(...). WorldObject::
GetEluna returns nullptr when the creature is not in the world, and
Creature::Update can still reach AI()->UpdateAI for such a creature (the core
itself notes "can be despawned by update pool"). The result was a SIGSEGV in
Eluna::UpdateAI on the first member read (this == nullptr):

  Eluna::UpdateAI(Creature*, unsigned int)+0x18
  ElunaCreatureAI::UpdateAI(unsigned int)+0xba
  Creature::Update(unsigned int, unsigned int)+0xdd5
  Map::UpdateCellsAroundObject(...)

Seen on 1181dev 96b87eb with one Lua-scripted creature (entry 14428, hooks
1/2/5/7/23), spawned by hand with .npc add. Each hook now treats a missing
state as "not handled", so the creature behaves like one with no script,
which is what ElunaScriptBridge already does for every other hook
(if (Eluna* e = x->GetEluna())).

Base: ElunaLuaEngine/Eluna 1b06f28ff3a00054d915d824c725fb4283fee74d (branch
cmangos-spell-update), the dep/Eluna pin, with patches 0001-0006 applied. Eluna is
GPL-3.0 (https://github.com/ElunaLuaEngine/Eluna, LICENSE); this change is under
the same licence. Applied by cmake/ElunaSources.cmake to a copy in the build tree.

